  "query_preview": "..\nA Typhoon Watch, Flash Flood Watch, and Coastal Flood Watch are now \nin effect for the Marianas. Fairly quiet conditions are expected to \ncontinue through Saturday morning, but expect to start seeing swaths \nof upper-level cirrus streaming over the islands, ahead of Typhoon \nBavi. Showers will begin to increase Saturday evening as the far \nouter rain bands of Bavi begin to move overhead, then, northerly \nwinds will begin to increase Saturday overnight. Regardless of where \nTyphoon Bavi eventually makes passage through the Marianas, \nconditions will begin to rapidly degrade for all islands Sunday, as \ntropical storm conditions begin to be felt. The timeframe and exact \npoint of passage remain uncertain and will see adjustment in the \nforecast over the next 36 to 48 hours, but there is higher confidence\nin Bavi arriving as a strong typhoon, potentially a Category 5 Super\nTyphoon with sustained winds potentially reaching 160 mph near the \ncenter. See the Tropical Systems section for more details.",
